<[John] JDHALL> Yerk stands for Yerkes as in Yerkes Observatory at U of Chicago.
<GARY-S> It is the original Object Oriented Language written in Forth, but as 
Neon lacked garbage collection
<[John] JDHALL> Bob Lowenstein got permission to put Yerk in the public domain..
<[John] JDHALL> Yes, it was formarly called Neon.  he has brought the version 
up....
<GARY-S> His group were using it at the Observatory and thought their version 
desreved   wider distribution
<[John] JDHALL> from 2.2 to now 3.3.2.  He ia an astronomer at Yerkes and the 
Flying Observatory
<[John] JDHALL> that flies out of Moffet field in CA.  ...
<GARY-S> Apple users "should" get a copy
<[John] JDHALL> I have talked to him and he uses it for all of his observing.   
...
<[John] JDHALL> As an example, U of Chicago has a "remote" observatory in New 
Mexico...
<[John] JDHALL> and a couple of weeks ago over New Zealand...
<[John] JDHALL> he disn't have anything to observe on the plane, so thru modem 
and ...
<[John] JDHALL> internet he was able to control the NM observatory and get 
pictures which...
<[John] JDHALL> he compressed and transmitted to the plane.  All this done in 
Yerk and all...
<[John] JDHALL> this communication occured in less than 15 minutes.  He has a 
compression...
<D.POPE7> is here.
<[John] JDHALL> technique that can compress  and effectively transmit at 37.?K 
bytes per sec. ..
<[John] JDHALL> He does all the programming himself.
